    "ori_content": {
      "type": "ori-collection-content",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "About the range",
        "show_title": false,
        "help_text": "Not sure what fits your truck? Our team can help you choose.",
        "help_label": "Contact our team",
        "help_link": "#tab-4",
        "text": "<h2>Silverado 2500 GVM Upgrade Options for Enhanced Towing Power</h2><p>One of the biggest challenges when you’re heading off the beaten track or out to a jobsite is making sure you can take all your gear, without overloading the manufacturer payload. When you want to be able to tow your trailer, boat, caravan, or simply load up the tub with more tools, you need some serious capabilities that won’t impact the structure or safety of your Chevy.</p><p>Our range of upgrades spans a huge scope of specs, giving you something custom, road-safe, and anywhere up to a 198% payload increase. Haul more and go further while still maintaining all the things you love about your truck when you get an engineered and installed Silverado GVM upgrade.</p><h2>Chevrolet Silverado 2500HD GVM Upgrades for Maximum Performance</h2><p>If you own a Chevy, you already know they’re an impressive beast both on and off the road. When you want to not only maintain their performance, but maximise it, Silverado GVM upgrades can help get you there. Between the boosted wheelbase from upgraded <a href=\"/collections/suspension\">suspension</a>, to more structural support from the new shocks and control arms, you’ll get better ground clearance, improved traction, and a structurally sound setup. These upgrades mean that you can carry your gear without strain - even on tough terrain.</p><p>When you transform your truck with a GVM package from ORI, you’ll also be able to add other upgrades that enhance the utility, functionality and personality of your vehicle. Get a fresh set of wheels to match the hauling power you’ve got, add on new <a href=\"/collections/bushwacker\">fender flares</a> to keep the undercarriage of your truck clear from dirt, or install a <a href=\"/collections/titan-fuel-tanks\">long range fuel tank</a> so you can go further. Silverado GVM upgrades do more than give you greater hauling power, they open you up to a whole new way to drive and enhance your truck.</p><h2>Silverado GVM Upgrade Packages – Enhance Your Vehicle’s Off-Road Capability</h2><p>When you’re offroading, sometimes you have to make a choice between taking all the gear you want with you or sticking to an easier path. If you’re too overloaded, handling, control, and stability can be impacted - but all of these concerns are alleviated with carefully engineered and installed <a href=\"/pages/ori-gvm-upgrades\">GVM upgrades</a>.</p><p>Our range enables you to lift your ground clearance by up to 6.5 inches, making it easier to tackle rugged tracks, beat your own path through the terrain, and maintain the traction you want.</p><h2>Silverado 2500 GVM Upgrade – Strengthen Your Vehicle for Heavy Duty Use</h2><p>Aside from the occasions when you need to be hauling higher loads, a GVM upgrade with ORI gives you a more resilient, hard-wearing truck regardless of what you’re carrying. You can tackle tough ground more easily, get through dry or soggy conditions with greater ease, and maintain a smooth ride no matter where you go and how much you’ve got in the tub.</p><p>No matter what motivates you, how you like to drive, or what you demand from your truck, a Chevy Silverado 2500HD GVM upgrade from ORI offers you the driving experience you’ve always wanted. Explore the range now, and if you’re unsure which option is right for you, you can contact us for a personal recommendation.</p><p>After you’ve purchased your upgrade, you can get everything installed and engineered and discover the difference it’ll make to your Chevy in a real-world environment. No matter whether you’re driving for work or play, you can head off with confidence knowing your Silverado can handle everything without compromising the handling, comfort, and control you’re used to.</p>",
        "collapse": true,
        "collapsed_height": 420,
        "more_label": "Read more",
        "less_label": "Read less",
        "tinted": true,
        "padding_top": 72,
        "padding_bottom": 72
      }
    },
    "ori_faq": {
      "type": "ori-gvm-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is a GVM upgrade and why do I need one?",
            "answer": "<p>Gross Vehicle Mass (GVM) is the maximum your Silverado can legally weigh when fully loaded—including the truck, passengers, fuel, accessories (like bull bars and canopies), and tow ball weight. If you are towing heavy or building a touring rig, the factory payload gets eaten up fast. Our GVM upgrades legally increase this limit so you can carry your gear without voiding your insurance or risking hefty fines.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does \"Pre-Rego\" and \"SSM Approval\" mean?",
            "answer": "<p>SSM stands for Second Stage of Manufacture. When we upgrade your truck <em>before</em> it is registered for the very first time (Pre-Rego), the federal government recognizes ORI as the secondary manufacturer. This means your massive lift, larger tyres, and upgraded GVM are baked into the truck's federal compliance plate. It is 100% legal to drive and insure in every state and territory in Australia.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will upgrading my GVM reduce my towing capacity?",
            "answer": "<p>Not with an ORI package. Some GVM upgrades force you to sacrifice towing capacity to carry more weight in the tub. Our Silverado 2500HD packages retain your factory 12,474 KG GCM (Gross Combination Mass), meaning you keep your full 4.5T braked towing capacity while maximizing your truck's payload.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does the NB1 to NB2 category upgrade mean?",
            "answer": "<p>By federal standards, NB1 vehicles are \"Light Goods Vehicles\" (under 4.5 tonnes). Our SSM packages legally reclassify your Silverado 2500HD as an NB2 \"Medium Goods Vehicle\" (over 4.5 tonnes). This reclassification is the secret to legally unlocking that massive 5500 KG–6000 KG GVM.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are 35-inch and 37-inch tyres actually legal on these builds?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes! If done Pre-Rego through our Stage 4, 5, 6, or 6.5 SSM packages, the larger tyre sizes are federally engineered and certified as part of the build. No state-based engineering headaches—just turn the key and drive your monster truck legally anywhere in the country.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is a Chevy Silverado GVM upgrade, and what are the benefits?",
            "answer": "<p>When you get a Chevy Silverado GVM upgrade, you take it from its factory settings to a whole new level of hauling power. The upgrade includes suspension and structural upgrades, incorporating new parts and accessories to enable you to carry more gear in the tub and cab – without overloading your truck, voiding your warranty and insurance, or compromising safety. You’ll get better ground clearance, exceptional control, and your Chevy will be able to handle more, no matter whether that’s on a jobsite or touring around Australia.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much additional payload can a Chevy Silverado GVM upgrade provide?",
            "answer": "<p>Depending on the package you go for, you can get into a 3 inch lift with a 133% increase in payload, ranging up to a mega 6.5 inch lift with a 192% payload increase. If you go for the maximum increase, your kerb weight payload will go all the way up to 2138 kgs. No matter what your motivation is for upgrading your Chevy Silverado’s GVM, there’s a package that’ll transform the way you drive.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will a GVM upgrade improve my Silverado's towing performance and stability?",
            "answer": "<p>To get improved towing capabilities, you can combine a GVM upgrade with a GCM upgrade. GVM specifically refers to the carrying capacity of your tub and cab, while a GCM upgrade supports towball weight capacity. The benefit of upgrading with Offroad Industries is that we can enable you to enhance the components you need, according to what you want from your Chevy. </p><p>Regardless of whether you go for a Chevy Silverado GCM upgrade, you will get improved stability, better handling, and greater ground clearance from a GVM upgrade. You’ll be able to load up the tub, head out, and still get the traction, power, and exceptional capabilities you demand of a working vehicle.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I install a Chevy Silverado GVM upgrade before or after registration?",
            "answer": "<p>All of our Chevy Silverado GVM upgrades need to be completed pre-rego to give you a fully compliant, nationally recognised GVM rating. It involves changing the rating from an NB1 to the heavy-duty NB2 category, and your truck will also require new wheels and types to match the increased power and weight-hauling capabilities of your truck.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_10": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is a Chevy Silverado GVM upgrade legal and certified in Australia?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, if it’s completed pre-rego, our Chevy Silverado GVM upgrades are fully legal throughout Australia. They’ve been thoroughly tested and engineered to deliver the power, safety, and legal compliance required to travel throughout every state and territory in Australia, no matter which stage you go for.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_11": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why choose Offroad Industries for a Chevy Silverado GVM upgrade?",
            "answer": "<p>When you want a serious upgrade, you want it engineered by a team who knows what they’re doing, which is exactly what you get with Offroad Industries. We specialise in parts, accessories and upgrades for American-made vehicles and our range of GVM upgrades for your Chevy Silverado is no exception. Every package we offer here is engineered and tested under exclusive SSM Approvals, giving you a genuinely powerful upgrade that goes beyond a lift alone.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_12": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What other American truck GVM upgrades does Offroad Industries offer?",
            "answer": "<p>Along with a broad scope of GVM upgrades for your Chevy Silverado 1500 and 2500, we cater to all of Australia’s favourite American-made vehicles. Find options for the <a href=\"/pages/ford-150-gvm-packages\">Ford F150</a>, <a href=\"/pages/ram-2500hd-5th-gen-gvm\">RAM 2500HD 5th gen</a>, and the latest RAM 2500 6th gen. Every package has been carefully engineered and tested for each model to ensure compliance, compatibility, and the maximum benefit for you every time you head out.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_13": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are Chevy Silverado GVM upgrades becoming more popular for touring and towing in Australia?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely. As more Australians invest in beasts like the Chevy Silverado, they want to max out the capabilities – and potential and the best way to do that is with a dedicated GVM upgrade. Whether it’s for carrying gear to the coast, attacking a rooftop tent setup when you’re heading into the bush, or just more power and payload for work, a Chevy Silverado GVM upgrade will get you there.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
